; transport-emit: built-in clock lanes (`:emit …`) under the corpus gate.
; beat/bar/phase broadcast straight from the transport env — the same
; numbers an `:expr` track binds, one f32 truncation at emission. An
; explicit (track :target beat …) overrides the emitted `beat` lane:
; emit lands FIRST, the track's write lands later and wins for in-order
; consumers (bar and phase have no track, so their emitted lane stands).
; :dur 1bar + :end hold pins the clamp edge — past the score length every
; lane freezes at the last tick, exactly as a keyed track clamps.
(transport :bpm 120 :meter [4 4] :dur 1bar :end hold :emit [beat bar phase])

(track :target beat
  (key :at 0b :value 10.0)
  (key :at 4b :value 20.0))
